WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.300
- [Narrator] This Great Big Story was

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:05.003
made possible by Japan Airlines.

00:00:06.442 --> 00:00:08.410
(steady piano music)

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:12.410
(indistinct background chatter)

00:00:30.405 --> 00:00:33.738
(curtains sliding open)

00:00:36.474 --> 00:00:37.970
(speaking foreign language)

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:39.760
Choko's school in Tokyo, Japan,

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.680
teaches people how to be mascots,

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:46.410
because the business of
being a mascot is big.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:47.653
Really big.

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:51.430
Mascots in Japan aren't just for sports.

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:53.920
They're for police departments, towns,

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.670
malls, airlines, even prisons.

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:59.600
They're a staple of Japanese culture.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:02.120
In Osaka alone, at one time there was

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.773
one mascot per 6,000 residents.

00:01:07.226 --> 00:01:10.893
(jaunty instrumental music)

00:01:16.916 --> 00:01:18.333
- One, two, jump.

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:21.700
- [Narrator] So she teaches them to wave,

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.873
to dance, to pose,

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.490
and her class is diverse.

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:31.060
He's a former chef.

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:32.570
She's a housewife.

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:35.450
This guy, he is a professional mascot.

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:39.060
Their ultimate goal, it's to perform.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:41.240
But of course, there are rules.

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:42.733
Number one: no talking.

00:01:53.556 --> 00:01:56.223
Number two: don't show any skin.

00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:09.893
Number three: don't be rude.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:13.280
These rules are here for one reason:

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:16.745
a mascot is more than just a costume.

00:02:16.745 --> 00:02:19.314
(speaking foreign language)

00:02:19.314 --> 00:02:21.397
(laughs)

00:02:34.506 --> 00:02:36.190
Being a mascot is about becoming

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:38.100
something greater than yourself.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:40.250
You can escape into the character.

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:42.803
In fact, that's what
you're supposed to do.

00:02:53.115 --> 00:02:56.690
Choko's been doing this for over 30 years,

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:58.940
and her students, well, they seem

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:00.540
like they're on the right track.

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:03.153
Keep on practicing, guys.

00:03:04.395 --> 00:03:08.228
(singing in foreign language)

00:03:09.936 --> 00:03:12.274
(clapping)

00:03:12.274 --> 00:03:15.357
(musical note plays)

